cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SafeStreets Walkability Methodology"
message: "If you use this methodology or the bundled datasets, please cite this repository."
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-02"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/Poseidon-t/walkability-methodology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Poseidon-t/walkability-methodology"
authors:
  - name: "Streets & Commons"
    website: "https://streetsandcommons.com"
abstract: >-
  Open methodology and supporting datasets behind the SafeStreets
  walkability score, a 4-component framework (Daily Reach, Street Safety,
  Transit Reach, Walking Comfort) rooted in the 15-minute city model.
  Combines OpenStreetMap, Sentinel-2 satellite imagery, EPA, US Census
  ACS, CDC PLACES, FEMA, NASADEM, Transitland GTFS, and Open-Meteo CAMS.
  Provides composite walkability scores for any address worldwide.
keywords:
  - walkability
  - pedestrian safety
  - 15-minute city
  - urban planning
  - street design
  - transit access
  - open data
  - OpenStreetMap
  - Sentinel-2
  - methodology
